288-- SCOPE: worktree `.temp/TASK-260822-4p3dcq/worktree`, branch `task/TASK-260822-4p3dcq-docs-build-ssh` off `origin/main` 6a9b201, carrying the accepted `96m5pj + 2505vo + 3pkc80 + b0wg3a` chain applied verbatim from `TASK-260822-b0wg3a_final.patch` and staged as the baseline. Delta charged to this task: `docs/build-ssh.md` (new, 494 lines) and one README bullet. No Go code touched.
289-- CORRECTION TO `b0wg3a` REVIEW FINDING 3 (the derived-default-outruns-its-validator trap): the general lesson holds, but the concrete case does not reproduce for `build_ssh`. The reviewer cited `identifiers.PortableComponent`, which is the `internal/identity` path governing *skill* sources. External build repositories parse through `buildrepo.ParseSource`, and for the SSH transport it restricts the raw repository path to `^[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$` (Spec §6.3) before Git or SSH starts — exactly the alphabet `scopeSegmentRE` admits. Verified at first hand: `ssh://git.example.com/team+infra/app.git` and `ssh://git.example.com/team@infra/app.git` are both refused at parse time with `repository SSH path must be portable ASCII`, and the scp form is refused by `scpRE`. So the *path* half of the divergence cannot occur on the only transport `build_ssh` ever selects for.
290:- WHAT DOES REPRODUCE, AND WHY THE PRESCRIBED REMEDY DOES NOT WORK: the divergence is in the **host**. `buildrepo.hostRE` is `^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.-]*$`; `config.scopeHostRE` requires non-empty dot-separated labels that neither start nor end with a hyphen. `ssh://git.example.com./team/app.git`, `ssh://git..example.com/...` and `ssh://git-.example.com/...` all parse to a valid canonical identity whose derived default scope the CLI refuses — **and whose host is not a valid scope either**, so "widen the suggestion to the host" does not rescue it. No `build_ssh` entry can cover such a repository at all; the covering path is `--build-ssh-agent`/`--build-ssh-identity` or `CURATOR_BUILD_SSH_*`. An HTTPS identity such as `git.example.com/team+infra/app` *does* carry a rejected namespace, but HTTPS repositories never reach the scope suggestion, so it is unreachable from the diagnostic.
291-- SPEC DRIFT WORTH KNOWING BEFORE ANYONE CITES IT: `profiles/manager.md §11.3` on `curator-spec` **main** still admits only two authentication tails. The third, pinned-agent tail this repository accepted in 6a9b201 lives on the unmerged branch `spec/pinned-agent-authentication-tail` (`38232d3`). CI `SPEC_PIN` is `00b1688`, which also predates it. The conformance corpus does not encode the tail, so no pin or checksum is affected — but a doc that presents three tails as settled protocol would be wrong today. `docs/build-ssh.md` says so explicitly.
292:- METHOD, HOW THE EXAMPLES WERE MADE NON-FICTIONAL: every transcript in the page came out of the implementation rather than a keyboard. CLI output from a binary built in the worktree against a scratch `CURATOR_CONFIG`; the `build_ssh` JSON block is that scratch file verbatim after four `add` calls; the seven fail-closed parse messages from seven hand-written malformed configs; the prompt transcript, both missing-credential diagnostics and the provenance line from a throwaway `docsample_test.go` in `internal/install` driving `resolveBuildSSH` and `InteractiveBuildSSHResolver` directly, captured and then deleted. Raw capture attached as `TASK-260822-4p3dcq_docsamples.log`.
