398:- DECISION: one predicate covers both AC skip cases — `needsBuildSSH` is `effective.IdentityKind == "network-git" && effective.Transport == "ssh"` (`internal/install/buildssh.go:158`). Reading the **effective** state rather than the declared one makes substitution decide the transport in both directions: a substitution redirecting a declared SSH repository onto HTTPS or a local path moves it off SSH, and one redirecting a declared HTTPS repository onto SSH moves it on. `TestSubstitutionMovesARepositoryOffAndOntoTheSSHTransport` pins both directions.
399-- DECISION: `GitTool.SSHCredentials` is bound **per repository** in `externalPipelineRequest`, never per run, so a closure spanning two hosts cannot offer either host the other's key (Spec §12.2). `AcquireNetwork` independently refuses an SSH source whose tool carries no selection (`internal/buildrepo/admission.go:261`) — the backstop for a caller that forgot to resolve, so no fetch can silently fall back to ambient SSH state.
400-- DECISION: `~/` expansion is **config-scoped only**, matching the AC wording. Flag/env values are not expanded; `ValidateOperatorSSHCredentials` requires an absolute path, so a `~/…` passed on the command line fails with "path must be absolute" rather than being silently reinterpreted. The shell already owns that expansion for a flag.
401-- DECISION: an entry recording `agent: true` with no socket resolves to the **live** `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, and errors when there is none rather than degrading to identity-only. A macOS agent socket is per login session, so a persisted path is the one thing a config cannot keep current. `known_hosts` resolves scope → run-wide → `$HOME/.ssh/known_hosts`; a run-wide `--build-ssh-known-hosts` governs a scoped selection too, because a scope selects authentication material, not who the destination is allowed to be.
