413-- ROOT CAUSE OF THE ONE FINDING WITH TEETH: `core.md` 4.1.1 states an **open criterion** for manager ownership of an environment name and delegates only the enumeration; `profiles/manager.md` 3.1 then declared its enumeration **closed**. A closed set that discharges an open criterion is only sound if it is provably complete — and over two interpreters and three platforms it was not: Linux enumerated three `LD_` names while macOS got `DYLD_` prefix closure, and Windows reserved `WINDIR` but not its twin `SystemRoot`. An `env_read` entry naming anything in the gap passed the caller's inherited value straight through, **fail-open and silent**, which is the exact hole the delegation existed to close.
